  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed side infill extension adjoining No.89 Durlston Road, by reason of its depth, height, bulk, and location, would have a harmful impact on the amenities of the neighbouring occupiers at No. 89 Durlston Road by way of a loss of outlook and sense of enclosure, and would have an overbearing impact.&amp;nbsp; As such, the proposed development is contrary to policies D6 (Housing quality and standards) of the London Plan (2021), policy LP2 (Development and Amenity) of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 (2020), and the guidance contained within Hackney&#x27;s Residential Extensions and Alterations SPD (2026).&amp;nbsp;",
    "The proposed dormer roof extension, by reason of its detailed design, scale, form, massing, and positioning, results in an incongruous, discordant and unsympathetic form of development that fails to respect the original architectural form of the host building and wider terrace, resulting in visual harm, failing to preserve or enhance the character and appearance of the Northwold and Cazenove Conservation Area. As such, the proposed development is contrary to policies D1 (London’s form, character and capacity for growth) and D3 (Optimising site capacity through the design-led approach) D4 (Good design) and HC1 (Heritage conservation and growth) of the London Plan (2021), policies LP1 (Design Quality and Local Character), LP3 (Designated Heritage Assets) of the Hackney Local Plan (2020) and Hackney&#x27;s Residential Extensions and Alterations SPD (2026)."
  ],
